SM(364,{"n":"Numbers 16","a":"Fr Stephen De Young Archives/Numbers 16.mp3","d":2745.2,"s":[[0.32,"Come and study the Holy Scriptures with us as Father Stephen DeYoung teaches verse by verse on the podcast The Whole Counsel of God."],[9.04,"Father Stephen holds a PhD in Biblical Studies, and is an Orthodox priest serving at Archangel Gabriel Orthodox Church in Lafayette, Louisiana."],[21.84,"We're gonna go ahead and get started, and uh when we get started, we're gonna be starting at the beginning of Numbers chapter 16."],[30.16,"And we'll have sort of minimal catch-up here because we mentioned last time this is becoming a refrain, but the book of Numbers has a whole bunch of different kinds of things in it."],[42.64,"It's not just numbers."],[44.64,"The uh everything from census data to commandments about different things to narrative stories of things happening to Israel in the desert, and it sort of shifts back and forth between these different genres and different types of. literature rapidly"],[63.96,"So chapter 15 that we talked about last time was a chapter that was made up of mostly commandments, so it was that type."],[78.28,"And now chapter 16 that we're going to read is also story again."],[82.04,"So I'm not going to go back through all the commandments we talked about last time."],[85.4,"People listening to this in the recording will see it."],[88.44,"But folks here who may not have been here last time will be okay because you don't need to know those commandments to understand the story we're about to start."],[96.96,"So but narratively, briefly, sort of where we are Israel has sort of been informed that they're now going. to spend the next 40 years in the desert"],[108.0,"So the rest of the book of Numbers, really, all of the narrative portions are going to be things that happened during that 40 years."],[116.96,"And there's nothing close to a continuous narrative of 40 years."],[121.84,"It's going to be very sp this happened, and then there's gonna be years that pass."],[126.48,"Here's another thing that happened years later."],[129.33,"So we're now just this is an incident that happened during this time."],[134.85,"And often we're not even given, like we' notre told how much time has passed."],[141.25,"We just know this is somewhere, somewhere during that 40 year period."],[146.69,"So, um that said, now that sort of minimal reintroduction, we can go ahead, we'll pick up, unless there's any leftover comments, questions, defenses of the Germans or the British royal family."],[161.93,"Uh, we'll go ahead and pick up in Numbers chapter 16, verse 1."],[169.29,"Now, Korah, the son of Isar, the son of Kohat, the son of Levi, and Dathan and Abiram, the sons of Eliab, and An, the son of Peleth, the son of Reuben, spoke."],[184.01,"Now, these sons of, this is a good example of a place."],[189.13,"We talked about this in the genealogies when it says this person begat that versus begat that person."],[193.69,"We talked. about how there are generations skipped"],[196.37,"So obviously there's a lot of generations skipped here."],[199.59,"Because remember, Levi is like Levi, the son of Jacob."],[205.68,"In Genesis. And we are more than three generations from the book of Genesis."],[211.78,"At this point."],[212.5,"A lot more than that."],[214.24,"So what these names that we're given are telling us, sort of in order, is we get their personal name, so Korah is the guy's personal name."],[225.12,"Izar is his father in the sense of that's the head of the big extended family that he's part of."],[233.04,"Who's the son of Kohat?"],[234.8,"That's the name of the clan that that family is a part of."],[238.28,"The clan of Kohat."],[240.2,"And then Levi is the tribe."],[242.62,"Out of the 12 tribes of Israel that he's a member of."],[245.66,"So this isn't literally like here's his dad's name and his granddad's name and his great granddad's name."],[251.66,"It's here's who he is, here's the family he's part of, and the clan he's a part of, and the tribe he's a part of."],[258.32,"In terms of the units of Israel."],[260.56,"They're the same thing we get with Dathan and Abiram."],[263.44,"They're part of the family of Eliab, who are part of the clan of On, and they're from Reuben."],[269.05,"But so Korah is a Levite, but uh Dathan and Abiram are not."],[277.45,"They're from the tribe of Reuben."],[279.93,"Verse 2, and they rose up before Moses with some of the children of Israel, 250 men of the children of Israel, rulers of the congregation, chosen members of the council, and men of note."],[289.97,"So they've got 250 guys."],[292.85,"Again, these are rough numbers, not precise, but this collection of people, and these aren't just sort of anybody who they rounded up, these are prominent people from different clans and different tribes."],[305.57,"They gathered together against Moses and Aaron and said to them, Let it be understood by you that all the congregation are holy ones, and the Lord is in them."],[314.69,"Why then do you exalt yourselves above the congregation of the Lord?"],[318.61,"So, Korah and these guys, the first Protestants."],[322.29,"I'm being mean, but little jab at our Protestant friends, but the argument they're making is right, all the Israelites are holy."],[332.41,"We're all God's people."],[334.81,"God speaks to all of us."],[336.89,"God leads all of us."],[338.41,"Who are you, Moses, to set yourself up as the leader?"],[342.49,"Who are you, Aaron, to say that you're the high priest and no one else gets to be the high priest?"],[346.89,"And your sons are the priests, and nobody else is a priest."],[350.89,"So I mean, kinda."],[354.75,"Like, we gotta be honest."],[358.03,"By the way, in in Jewish tradition, I found this out, I learned this recently."],[362.11,"In Jewish tradition, there's a saying, apparently, that the last time there was a dispute where one side was just 100% right and what uh the other side was 100% wrong."],[370.43,"and The last time that happened in human history was Moses Korah."],[378.47,"So as this unfolds, we're going to see."],[381.99,"One side here is clearly right, and one side is clearly wrong."],[385.29,"Now, their argument isn't based on nothing."],[388.25,"God did call them in Exodus to be a kingdom of priests, to exercise this kind of priesthood, all of the Israelites as this kind of priesthood for the other nations."],[397.61,"But then he also clearly designated certain people from certain tribes and certain clans and certain families for certain roles, within the larger camp and community."],[407.23,"There's authority, there's hierarchy here, and structure."],[412.45,"And that structure is what Korah and these people are attacking."],[414.61,"They're not just saying, oh, I want to be the high priest instead of you"],[420.09,"This isn't just we're gonna kick you guys out now I'm gonna take your place."],[424.09,"This is at least the argument they're making, that may be what they're wanting to do, but the argument they're making is that we should all be equal."],[433.61,"This should be a democracy."],[435.37,"Everyone should get to do all of these things."],[439.05,"But the accusation there, of course, no, implied is Moses and Aaron have taken these positions for themselves."],[447.45,"So they're denying or rejecting the idea that God placed them in authority, that the authority they have comes from God and asserting it doesn't, this is just something you've seized."],[461.57,"So when Moses heard this, he fell on his face."],[465.97,"And he spoke to Korah and all his company, saying, God examines and knows those who are his and who are his holy ones, and he brings them to himself, and those he chooses for himself, he brings to himself."],[481.41,"So what's Moses saying here?"],[483.74,"So Moses falls on his face."],[485.42,"Moses does this show of humility."],[488.64,"Because he understands the accusation."],[490.48,"Oh, you're falling the face."],[492.4,"Yeah, you're ambitious, Moses."],[494.02,"You're, you know, you're you're trying to lord it over us."],[496.58,"He's like, oh, no, far be free."],[498.4,"He says, and he says, you know, the authority, the people who are called to this, when he talks about coming close to God, this is very literal."],[503.28,"Because the high priest is the one who goes into the most holy place"],[508.42,"And the priests are the one who go into the holy place."],[510.43,"They get closer to God in a literal way."],[512.85,"But he's saying, God is the one who chooses who has this authority."],[518.87,"You don't just grasp it."],[525.19,"Put fire and incense in them before the Lord tomorrow, and it shall be that the man the Lord chooses, this is the holy one, and let this be sufficient for you, O sons of Levi."],[535.59,"So Moses says, Look, God chooses, so you guys show up, bring your censors, be ready to be priests, and if God chooses you to be priests, then you'll be priests."],[550.37,"If God chooses someone else, then you need to accept that."],[553.19,"Because God is the one who calls people."],[557.51,"Then Moses said to Korah, Hear me, you sons of Levi, is this a small thing to you that the God of Israel separated you from the congregation of Israel to bring you near to himself, to serve the liturgies of the Lord's tabernacle and to stand before the congregation to serve them."],[574.23,"And then he brought you near, you and all your brethren, the sons of Levi, with you."],[578.71,"Are you seeking the priesthood also?"],[581.27,"So he's talking now specifically to the Levites out of the group, Korah and the Levites."],[586.47,"So the folks from the tribe of Reuben are sort of in a different category."],[591.28,"But he's saying, look, you guys are you guys are Levites."],[594.48,"God called you to be Levites."],[596.16,"You have this special position compared to all the other tribes."],[599.04,"And God has given you this role in serving the liturgies."],[601.68,"And your family in particular has this particular role that God has given you."],[606.08,"You just that's nothing to you."],[608.34,"That's that's nothing."],[609.86,"Like you you want to try and seize the priesthood also?"],[613.06,"Like, if you can't have that, then forget the whole thing."],[617.94,"Because in this case, it it's it's this is the area where it's especially concerning."],[623.8,"In that it's not that God hasn't given them any role."],[629.08,"They that God's called them to do something and they want something else."],[633.36,"Because they consider it better or more prestigious or whatever."],[635.0,"Thus, you and all your company brought together are against God"],[642.72,"Furthermore, who is Aaron that you murmur against him?"],[645.86,"So he says, first of all, like you're disputing with God."],[648.58,"God gave you something to do, and you're saying, No, I don't want that."],[651.06,"I want this other thing."],[652.9,"So you're arguing with God."],[654.34,"And then also, by the way, what did Aaron ever do to you?"],[658.2,"Like, why why are you coming after him?"],[660.8,"Um. He's just serving the way God has called him to."],[665.84,"He he hasn't, like, he didn't take the high priesthood from you."],[669.54,"Like, he's he's just trying to serve God."],[674.26,"Then Moses sent to call Dathan and Abiram the sons of Eliab."],[677.78,"So now he's that he was addressing the Levites who are part of the group"],[678.86,"Okay. Now he's trying to talk to the others."],[684.8,"So he summons them to come talk to him."],[687.52,"The Levites were around because Moses is a Levite."],[690.98,"Aaron is a Levite."],[692.1,"They're all camped together."],[694.02,"So he says, send, you know, these guys who are part of this group, who are the leaders who aren't Levites, have them come see me."],[702.9,"But they said, We will not come up."],[705.46,"Is this a small thing that you brought us up out of a land flowing with milk and honey to kill us in the desert and set yourself over us as a ruler?"],[713.14,"Let's pause. So there's there's a well, there's a bunch of problems here."],[716.58,"So notice how they kind of parody what Moses said to Korrah."],[722.62,"Oh, do you think it's nothing?"],[723.98,"You know, do you think it's nothing that you were given?"],[725.9,"Oh, do you think it's nothing?"],[727.26,"That you brought us up and Egypt is now a land flowing with milk and honey."],[732.22,"Oh. Was that what Egypt was like for them?"],[735.42,"Really? You brought us out of land flowing with milk and honey."],[738.86,"And and notice."],[740.12,"This doesn't even make logical sense."],[742.28,"You brought us out here to kill us in the desert and to make yourself a ruler over us."],[748.44,"How do you do both of those things?"],[754.12,"Is he a tyrant who wants to like rule them all, or is he trying to kill them all?"],[759.4,"Then verse 14 Even if you should bring us into a land flowing with milk and honey and give us an inheritance of field and vineyards, you would put out the eyes of these men, we will not come up."],[770.64,"So he says, Oh, even if you are playing, you know, try if you are who you say you are and doing what you claim, you know, if if we send the two leaders of this this rebellion to you, you're gonna gouge out their right, you're gonna do something horrible to them to take your revenge, because you're this petty tyrant."],[788.69,"Because because that's what Moses has done a whole bunch of times."],[792.61,"Yes, gouged out people's eyes, tortured people, anyone who anyone who disagrees with them, Moses just takes out."],[800.91,"As opposed to what we've seen over and over and over again, which is God is ready to destroy the people in their rebellion, and Moses is there interceding in praying and asking God to have mercy on them."],[810.59,"And they're they're accusing Moses of the exact opposite"],[815.89,"So this is this is pure like derangement."],[819.33,"This is just pure we hate Moses."],[821.71,"Because like it doesn't even make sense."],[823.63,"Like the different accusations don't make sense together."],[827.77,"Like, there's no there's no logical case being made here."],[832.73,"Then Moses was very heavy of spirit and said to the Lord, May you pay no attention to their sacrifice."],[839.13,"I have not taken a desirable object from any of them, nor have I harmed any of them."],[844.81,"Okay, so Moses says to God, you know, tomorrow when they come with the incense."],[852.17,"Please don't accept it."],[853.69,"And then he says, I haven't done any bad thing to any of these people to have them hate me this way."],[860.01,"And I haven't taken anything from like he's not like taking their money, taking their possess."],[865.87,"Like he's not, he's like, you know, God, I'm not getting rich off of this."],[869.23,"I haven't done anything to any of them."],[870.99,"I don't understand why they hate me."],[873.15,"Then Moses said to Korah, Sanctify your company and be ready tomorrow before the Lord, you and they as well as Aaron."],[881.47,"Let each take his censer, put incense in it, and bring his censor before the Lord, two hundred and fifty censors, both you and Aaron, each with his censor."],[890.83,"Okay, so he says, God, God will choose."],[894.29,"Who's gonna be who's and tell us who's right."],[896.85,"So every man took his censor, put fire in it, laid incense in it, and stood at the doors of the tabernacle of testimony with Moses and Aaron"],[904.41,"Thus Korah gathered all his company against them at the door of the tabernacle of testimony."],[909.29,"Then the glory of the Lord appeared to all the congregation."],[912.57,"Okay, so they all gather."],[914.58,"Korra and all his people are in front of the entrance to the tabernacle."],[919.22,"Aaron and the priest from his family and stuff are there in the courts of the tabernacle."],[925.62,"And God appears."],[927.62,"The Lord then spoke to Moses and Aaron, saying, Separate yourselves from among this congregation, and I will utterly destroy them at once."],[935.54,"So he says, Moses, Aaron, back up."],[938.22,"Because I'm about to I'm about to wipe them all out."],[941.9,"Then they fell on their faces and said, O God, the God of the spirits and of all flesh, if one man sin, will the Lord's anger be on all the congregation."],[950.86,"So notice what they do."],[953.82,"They don't say."],[955.34,"Yeah, they don't just take two big steps back and like rub their hands together and be like, Yeah, see?"],[961.58,"This is what happens when you mess with us."],[963.18,"No, once again, Moses and Aaron pray and intercede and say, Hey, you know, yeah, Korah's way out of line, but don't hold that against everybody."],[974.38,"Even though they're all gathered there with him, they're all on his side."],[977.3,"They're all. Then the Lord spoke to Moses, saying, Speak to the congregation, saying, Withdraw from around Korah's company."],[986.82,"So God's response is, okay, tell them all also to take a big step back away from Korah and his guys."],[995.38,"Moses then rose and went to Dathan and Abiram, and the elders of Israel went together with him."],[1001.14,"Then he spoke to the congregation, saying, Get away from the tents of those callous men."],[1005.7,"Touch nothing of theirs lest you perish together with them in all their sin."],[1010.58,"So they're get away from them."],[1012.82,"By the way, don't try to take their stuff."],[1016.34,"This shows you just how human this is."],[1018.6,"That there would be some guy who's like, wait, God's gonna smite them?"],[1021.56,"Like, well, they're not gonna need this."],[1023.18,"Like, why don't I just grab that and uh take it with me?"],[1028.22,"So they got away from around Korah's tent, and Dathan and Abiram went and stood at the doors of their tents with their wives, their children, and their little ones."],[1036.02,"So even his fellow leaders are like, Yeah, you know what?"],[1040.02,"This isn't going how we thought it might."],[1043.54,"They back off."],[1044.68,"But Korah is apparently set in his ways."],[1047.56,"That's what the callous there means."],[1049.16,"The callous is hard or stubborn, is the idea there."],[1051.72,"Then Moses said, By this you shall know the Lord sent me to do all these works, and they are not from myself."],[1057.72,"Okay, so it says, I'm gonna give you a sign."],[1060.22,"So that everyone in Israel knows I didn't take this authority for myself."],[1064.14,"This has nothing to do with me."],[1065.66,"God put me in this position and gave me right this authority."],[1071.1,"If these men should die naturally, like all men, or if they are visited by the common visitation of all men, then the Lord has not sent me."],[1075.02,"by But the Lord will show a sign from heaven that opening its mouth, the earth shall swallow them down with their houses, their tents, and everything belonging to them, and they shall go down alive into Hades."],[1090.98,"Then you shall know these men provoke the Lord."],[1093.78,"So here's a sign."],[1100.71,"Going down into the underworld."],[1102.95,"They're gonna die, and their spirits go to the underworld like earth crack open."],[1108.67,"right Right? They're falling down in there."],[1110.95,"Now, as he finished speaking, all these words, the ground split apart under them, and the earth opened and swallowed them down with their houses, and all the men with Korah and all their tents."],[1119.35,"So they they all went with them, went down alive into Hades, and the earth covered them, and perished from the midst of the congregation."],[1126.11,"Then all Israel around them fled at their cry, for they were saying, Lest the earth also swallow us down."],[1132.11,"Fire also came out from the Lord and consumed the 250 men offering incense."],[1136.83,"So there's a certain irony there."],[1140.37,"You offer incense by burning it."],[1144.61,"Yeah. So were they offering the incense while all that was happening?"],[1149.25,"Yes. They were at the gate of the tabernacle."],[1152.37,"Like they didn't repent, kind of thing."],[1154.29,"Yeah. Yeah. So they get the Nadab and Abahu treatment."],[1159.35,"But Korah. Now, that said, one of the interesting things that we're going to see later on in the Old Testament is that in the book of Psalms, there's a whole series of psalms right before and right after 100, in the way it's currently compiled, that are written by the sons of Korah."],[1178.43,"Same Korah. And when you read the contents of a bunch of those psalms, they talk about God preserving them from falling down into going down into Hades."],[1192.05,"Going down into Sheol."],[1193.51,"Going down into the underworld."],[1195.67,"And the idea here is that those surviving members of Korah's household had this experience of being delivered from the consequences of rebellion. and sin"],[1209.95,"And so they poetically, in these psalms that have been preserved for us, these hymns that are preserved of us, sort of preserve that experience."],[1220.51,"That experience of being in rebellion against God, being in sin, realizing you're on your way to somewhere you don't want to be."],[1229.8,"And being rescued from that, being preserved from that."],[1233.8,"Because from the perspective of the Old Testament, this is not God punishing these people because they did something bad."],[1245.64,"This is these people receiving the consequences of their actions."],[1251.64,"Nadab at Abahu came sinfully into the presence of God."],[1252.92,"came. These people sinfully into the presence of God to offer incense"],[1260.4,"And in their wickedness, God's holiness consumed them."],[1264.42,"Like fire. Who said, no, you know what?"],[1275.24,"Uh I'm gonna dist literally, I'm going to distance myself from Korah."],[1279.3,"They repented. And so they didn't suffer that consequence."],[1285.64,"But those who were committed, fully committed to that, end up receiving the consequence, of their actions, which is death, which is destruction."],[1297.77,"And we have to keep in mind, why, because we've seen several cases of this."],[1305.11,"Last time it was a guy who gathered sticks on the Sabbath."],[1308.21,"We've seen a bunch of examples of this where somebody has sort of made an object lesson."],[1313.33,"And from our perspective, we have a very individualistic perspective as modern people."],[1318.93,"And so we read a story like this."],[1321.33,"Well, from Kora's perspective, though, you can kind of understand what he was saying."],[1325.49,"And, you know, did he really deserve that?"],[1327.97,"You know, that's kind of mean of God, to you know."],[1331.7,"But if we accept the reality that re rebbelliellionon aga againstinst God God has has as its end, living a life in of sin and wickedness as its end destruction."],[1346.43,"Then these people who were leaders in the community were trying to lead the whole community to destruction."],[1353.31,"That would have been the consequence of them getting their way."],[1357.39,"And them setting themselves up as leader."],[1360.19,"Would have been the whole congregation, going to destruction."],[1367.03,"And so God displaying the consequences in the here and now as a sign."],[1374.23,"Here's a sign of where this leads."],[1377.11,"With these people who were the instigators, then sends a message to everyone else to repent."],[1385.63,"So, spiritually speaking, the death of these 250 people, saves the lives of thousands of people."],[1393.57,"And that's the dynamic that the text is expressing."],[1399.97,"And we're not told that every member of Korra's group, we may read, you know, oh, went down into Hades, oh, that means they went to hell."],[1407.95,"That's not what that means."],[1409.15,"It just means they're dead."],[1411.63,"Because from the perspective of the Torah, everybody dies and goes to Sheol."],[1415.73,"Everybody dies and goes to the underworld."],[1417.33,"We don't know what's going to happen to them in the future on the day of judgment."],[1421.01,"We know Korra was dead wrong, because this pretty much shows us he was dead wrong."],[1425.73,"But that doesn't necessarily mean that this is like an unpardonable sin in the grander eternal sense."],[1433.53,"And we definitely don't know the people other than Korra who are part of this group, every individual, what the status of their life relationship with God."],[1443.29,"We just know they were very wrong about this one thing."],[1446.57,"And that because of the danger that represented, there had to be a sign given for the sake of everyone else."],[1454.01,"But so this is there's there seems to be this sort of prejudice."],[1460.43,"I I saw this recently."],[1462.63,"One of these internet atheists, you know, like, oh, there was a flood in Texas and people died, therefore God doesn't exist."],[1471.15,"Like, bad thing happened, therefore no God"],[1471.59,"There's a bunch of unstated premises there."],[1476.84,"Like, what? So in response to that, you you get a lot of weird arguments from people who identify themselves as Christians to either deny that those things are bad things."],[1490.2,"It's like, no, a lot of people dying in a flood is bad."],[1494.38,"That's a bad thing that happened."],[1496.54,"Or trying to say somehow God wasn't involved in it."],[1501.18,"Like, but that's not a mature understanding, of the way the the world works."],[1509.68,"Um the the atheist is assuming that you know if there's a God, then he's responsible for all the bad things that happen."],[1514.56,"there's But he doesn't believe a God, so according to him, who's responsible for all the bad things?"],[1525.16,"And why can't they be responsible if there is a God?"],[1529.66,"Like, that doesn't make a lot of sense."],[1532.38,"But even more than that, what the scriptures tell us, scripture talks about these bad things that happen."],[1539.66,"Tells us about wars and massacres and plagues and right that these things happen."],[1545.1,"And it shows us in various ways how, in the grand scheme of things, God brings good out of them."],[1551.58,"Or they serve purposes."],[1554.95,"And the fact, the reality of the resurrection of the dead that we believe in as Christians, that everyone will be raised up on the last day, means that whatever happens, good and bad in this world, that's not the final word on human existence and human life."],[1576.07,"And so these are all things we need to take into account."],[1580.52,"But there will be people who will come and say, oh, this is one of these horrible things that the Old Testament God does."],[1587.08,"One of these horrible things."],[1589.21,"But wh whyy is it a horrible thing?"],[1591.77,"I mean, it's certainly a b badad thing happens to Korah and 250 other people."],[1597.02,"But what makes that a bad thing in the grander scheme of things?"],[1601.42,"What makes that a bad thing for the sons of Korah later, as they're reflecting on it?"],[1605.54,"What makes that a bad thing for the rest of the Israelites?"],[1609.54,"What makes that a bad thing for Moses and Aaron who are being falsely accused of all kinds of things?"],[1617.62,"We need to move past just this kind of individualist perspective and this weird fantasy world of I'm a beautiful and unique snowflake, and no one like me has ever lived, and I deserve to have nothing but candy and rainbows my whole life."],[1634.42,"Nothing bad should happen to me."],[1636.88,"I mean, grow up."],[1639.88,"'s not that That's not a mature view of how the world works."],[1643.36,"It's not a mature view of who I am and my own sinfulness and my own wickedness and the ways I need to learn and I need to grow and I need to face consequences for my own actions."],[1654.52,"This idea that God should be this sort of indulgent parent is is ridiculous, especially if you've seen the children of indulgent parents and how they tend to turn out."],[1666.84,"So these are all things to keep in mind when we read passages like this."],[1671.9,"And questions to ask."],[1673.1,"What is God doing in terms of the collective communal life of the people as a whole here?"],[1678.54,"Sometimes when people are engaging in particularly destructive activity and going around getting other people on their side and to engage in it with them, sometimes it needs to be displayed what the consequences of that are for the sake of everyone else."],[1697.86,"That's just a reality."],[1699.63,"That's a reality in our life too."],[1701.79,"That's a reality in a parent's life who's raising children."],[1704.75,"They need to do that sometimes."],[1706.35,"That's a reality in our culture and society in terms of the application of the law and the court system."],[1711.87,"Sometimes you need to throw the book at somebody."],[1714.13,"Like, because what they've done has this significant larger impact on more than just them themselves."],[1721.47,"We need to look at this bigger, this bigger picture."],[1727.01,"This bigger picture."],[1729.25,"The story isn't over yet."],[1731.09,"It's gonna get worse before it gets better."],[1733.09,"Spoilers. But you've had fair warning now the Lord spoke to Moses and to Eliezer the son of Aaron the priest take up the copper censors out of the midst of those burned up and scatter the strange fire there so as to sanctify the censors of those sinners even the censors of the men who sinned at the cost of their lives and make them into beaten plates as a covering for the altar so they might be brought before the Lord and sanctified to become a sign to the children of Israel so go and collect all the censors, dump all the incense out."],[1768.05,"That's the strange fire."],[1769.11,"Get rid of that."],[1770.15,"And notice so as to sanctify the censors of those sinners."],[1776.07,"What is uh what is the image we're being given here of forgiveness?"],[1783.35,"Sensors aren't punished."],[1785.28,"The sensors are cleansed, they're purified."],[1788.34,"Dump the incense out of them."],[1790.02,"The incense was the problem."],[1791.46,"These are people who weren't supposed to be offering incense."],[1793.96,"So you dump the incense out."],[1796.76,"Is it an implication that they were actually offering their own kind of incense to?"],[1800.68,"Or like kind of like made that."],[1802.26,"They weren't the people, and they that, yeah."],[1805.22,"Yeah, yeah. And so once that's gone, and so this is an image of sin being removed from a person."],[1813.81,"Forgiveness is the removal, the washing away, the purification from sin."],[1818.21,"And then they're to take the copper sensors. and beat them all out into a covering for the altar"],[1825.55,"Okay? This is gonna be assigned to the people of Israel."],[1828.99,"Question. Now it says assigned to the people of Israel."],[1832.75,"You immediately might think, oh, well, this way they'll remember Korah."],[1837.55,"And they won't make the same mistake."],[1839.33,"The whole object lesson thing."],[1840.61,"Like, oh yeah, they'll see that, be like, oh yeah, I remember that Korah guy that's made from the censors."],[1845.86,"That priestly authority is something God gives."],[1848.26,"You don't try to claim that, you don't try to take that for yourself."],[1852.76,"That that's what's going on there."],[1854.52,"But when would the people have seen the covering of the altar?"],[1862.56,"Of incense. The priest and the high priests."],[1864.68,"Because this is the holy place, altar of incense"],[1867.49,"So who is this actually a reminder to?"],[1871.33,"The priests. That's why he has the priests make it, because they're the only ones who could go in there and attach it."],[1878.11,"This is a reminder to the priests about Korah."],[1882.77,"So the priests are being reminded."],[1884.85,"The people just saw this."],[1886.67,"So they know this story."],[1888.81,"But the priests are being reminded the calling you have is from God."],[1893.45,"Because being given authority, as we've talked about before, is this double-edged sword, and we don't think about it that way."],[1900.73,"People coming at this like Korah want the prestige, want to be in charge, want the letters before and after their name."],[1909.41,"They don't want the responsibility that comes with it, the judgment that comes with it."],[1915.49,"That St. Paul reaffirms when he says, not many of you should presume to be teachers."],[1919.34,"Because God is going to hold more accountable."],[1921.84,"The more authority God gives you, the more accountable He holds you."],[1925.36,"We've talked about this before in the Bible study."],[1927.78,"Like when each of us stands before God on the day of judgment, we have to give an account for ourselves."],[1933.78,"If you're married, you have to give an account for yourself and your spouse."],[1938.18,"If you have children, you have to give an account for yourself, your spouse, and your children."],[1943.86,"If you're a priest, when I stand before Christ on the day of judgment, I have to give an account for myself, for my spouse, for every one of you."],[1951.14,"And everyone else in the parish"],[1958.7,"When the bishop stands before Christ on the day of judgment, he has to give an account for himself, for all of his clergy and their families, and for all of the people in every church that he oversaw."],[1972.14,"That's a heavy weight."],[1986.62,"And it goes around the back of his neck."],[1990.28,"And hangs down."],[1992.45,"Because this represents the authority. being this weight that he's taking on his shoulders"],[2002.97,"And so that's usually not the people who say, Well, why can't I do this?"],[2008.73,"Why can't I do that?"],[2009.77,"Why can't they accountability."],[2013.7,"They're not wanting the weight of that authority."],[2015.78,"They're not wanting the heaviness of it."],[2017.86,"They're not really wanting the responsibility."],[2020.58,"They're wanting the things they perceive from outside about it."],[2024.6,"People calling them by a title and asking them for a blessing."],[2029.1,"They don't want this other part."],[2031.42,"And so this is a reminder to the priests of that other part."],[2037.02,"Of the awesomenomeness ofess the and the. seriousness and the fears task God has given them"],[2045.2,"And the accountability that comes with that."],[2048.24,"Every time they see this made from the censors of false priests, they're going to be reminded of that responsibility."],[2059.12,"And Eliezer, the son of Aaron the priest, took the copper censors, which those burned up had brought, and they added those as a covering for the altar, as a memorial to the children of Israel, that no outsider who is not of Aaron's seed should put incense before the Lord and be like Korah and his insurrection, as the Lord said by the hand of Moses."],[2080.0,"So you might think, okay, well, issue dealt with."],[2083.04,"Everybody should be happy now"],[2084.29,"That's a pretty big display."],[2088.89,"But if you've been paying attention, our Israelite friends are not so quickly uh satisfied."],[2097.13,"Yeah. Uh they said they beat it into plates and made like are they talking about just kind of like uh like a cover or like a copper no like copper beaten out that they put as a covering around it would just be like something on top of it to protect it?"],[2114.73,"No, it'd be attached to it."],[2116.09,"Okay. To the sides of it."],[2117.61,"Okay. Yeah, yeah, yeah."],[2120.65,"The next day the children of Israel murmured against Moses and Aaron, saying, You killed the people of the Lord."],[2126.17,"the They just saw earth swallow a bunch of people and fire come out of the tabernacle and incinerate a bunch of people."],[2128.85,"Now this takes some guts."],[2139.49,"But still they have the chutzpah to come out and say, like, you know, those were good people."],[2150.58,"Those were good godly people who you killed Moses."],[2154.9,"So Moses was the one that opened up the water."],[2157.06,"Yes. Yes. Yes."],[2159.54,"Moses is an evil wizard, apparently."],[2165.3,"Now it happened when the congregation regrouped itself against Moses and Aaron."],[2170.06,"They hastened to the tabernacle of testimony, and the cloud covered it, and the Lord's glory was seen."],[2176.16,"So God's visiting again."],[2178.72,"And as we've commented before, when God visits his people in the Old and New Testaments, this isn't like grandpa coming over to visit."],[2186.48,"Yay! We're gonna play Scrabble."],[2191.32,"This is more like wait till your dad gets home."],[2195.8,"There's gonna be a reckoning now."],[2198.66,"So the chickens are coming home to roost again."],[2202.34,"Then Moses and Aaron entered the front of the tabernacle of testimony, and the Lord spoke to Moses and Aaron, saying, Get away from the midst of the congregation, and I will utterly destroy them at once."],[2212.6,"So God says, apparently they didn't get the message yesterday."],[2217.2,"So I guess some more of them are going to have to uh be an object lesson."],[2224.96,"So they fell on their faces, Moses and Aaron."],[2228.08,"So again, Moses and Aaron are interceding for the people."],[2232.32,"Now, as we've said before, this is not just, you know, there are people who want to portray this in this very literal and kind of silly way that God just like keeps flying off the handle and and he's like actually mad."],[2247.76,"Yeah, and like, oh, and and Moses and Aaron are like, now skeeter, we don't want no trouble."],[2253.7,"Like just relax, relax right's that's not at all right what going on here right this is God is doing this because Moses and Aaron are learning and growing too and part of this is again and again Moses and Aaron are learning and displaying this humility right more humility than I have like about the third time this happened and God said let me just wipe them out and you and me will start over, I'd be like, sounds good."],[2291.08,"I'd be like, yeah, I'm done too."],[2293.28,"You know. Like, but but that's not, I'm not Moses."],[2296.67,"I am not a saint like Moses."],[2298.57,"Because Moses again and again says, No, please don't."],[2302.09,"Yes, these people have gathered together again to try to murder me, but please, God, don't hurt them."],[2308.51,"Don't give them the consequence, don't give them what they deserve."],[2311.79,"Don't give them what they think they want."],[2314.11,"Don't. Please just have mercy on them."],[2318.64,"Moses again and again is finding this within himself."],[2322.56,"And this is transformative for Moses."],[2325.2,"Yeah. Yeah, who used to not be quite so forgiving earlier in his life."],[2330.08,"Then Moses said to Aaron, Take the censer, put fire in it from the altar, throw incense on it, and carry it quickly to the camp and make atonement for them."],[2338.96,"For wrath has gone out from the Lord's face and is beginning to strike the people."],[2343.92,"So he says to Aaron, you're the one who's the rightful priest."],[2350.63,"So go take incense from the altar in here in the tabernacle, put it in your censer, and go out there and publicly intercede for the people."],[2360.01,"So now the people are going to see Aaron, the one who God has made the high priest, standing in the midst of them, beseeching God for mercy for them."],[2370.83,"In the face of the judgment that they deserve that's coming upon them."],[2376.91,"Which is so there's an interesting dynamic here."],[2379.73,"Because just seeing the consequences, apparently the day before didn't teach them what they needed to learn."],[2387.62,"Uh so now this is a different approach that we're taking."],[2393.14,"And God has brought Moses to coming up with this approach."],[2398.12,"God doesn't tell Moses to do this."],[2400.92,"Moses comes up with this is what we need to do for them to maybe understand."],[2407.22,"That we're on their side."],[2409.64,"We're not the ones they need to be angry at."],[2412.28,"We're not the ones they should be hating."],[2413.88,"We're right, day by day."],[2415.88,"And the position of high priest is not lording it over them."],[2419.82,"Or ruling over them."],[2421.18,"You're interceding for them."],[2423.11,"Before God. That's what the high priest does."],[2426.17,"So do go do it publicly."],[2427.69,"Go do it in the middle of them so that they see it"],[2431.65,"So Aaron took it as Moses told him and ran into the assembly."],[2436.05,"And already the plague had begun among the people."],[2439.09,"So he threw in the incense and made atonement for the people."],[2443.09,"And he stood between the dead and the living, so the plague ceased."],[2447.89,"So at the place where he's standing and interceding, that's where sort of the death and destruction stops."],[2456.29,"So that makes a pretty public display."],[2458.85,"Notice also he made atonement for the people."],[2461.17,"So this means, of course, he murdered that incense and punished it for their sins."],[2467.86,"Does it make any sense?"],[2469.94,"What does the smoke of incense do?"],[2471.7,"It purifies. So atonement here again, he's purifying the people."],[2477.68,"From the results, from the consequence of their sin."],[2482.4,"Now those who died in the plague were 14,700 besides those who died because of Korah."],[2488.4,"Then Aaron returned to Moses at the door of the tabernacle of testimony, and the plague ceased."],[2494.24,"So here's another sign for you."],[2502.52,"A couple of times now here in Numbers."],[2505.8,"The book of Numbers is one of the interesting things about it is that these miracles that happen, these miraculous things that happen, and there's going to be more of them as we go forward in these stories set during this 40 years, are described as signs."],[2520.46,"Like the ten plagues of Egypt were also miraculous in various ways, but they aren't described as signs in the same way."],[2528.46,"That's a word that gets used here in Numbers."],[2532.22,"The reason I'm pointing that out is that's also a word that gets used in the Gospel of John in the New Testament for Christ's miracles."],[2542.22,"In the Synoptic Gospels in Matthew, Mark, and Luke, they're just described as miracles, as healings."],[2548.06,"That sign language isn't used."],[2550.78,"But that sign language is used in St."],[2555.1,"John's Gospel. And then there are also a bunch later on in Numbers, we're gonna get the whole episode with the bronze serpent getting lifted up in the wilderness that Christ refers to in St."],[2561.58,"So there are a lot of connections between what St"],[2563.22,"John's Gospel. John is doing in his gospel and the book of Numbers."],[2572.79,"In how he portrays Jesus' authority as being like the authority of Moses, but also how he portray is portraying life in this world and the 40 years in the wilderness."],[2588.23,"That our life in this world is sort of a sojourn."],[2591.37,"And into that life, certain signs from God enter through Christ, to teach us, to show us the path, the way through that lifetime in wandering in the wilderness, and and to teach us."],[2605.73,"Because this period of time in the wilderness, again, we we talked about before in the passage we're just talking about, this isn't just a punishment."],[2613.49,"The reason why why did we talk about the number 40?"],[2616.37,"What's 40 years?"],[2617.89,"It's a period of preparation, 40 days, 40 years, whenever you see 40."],[2622.53,"Because it's actually 42, and that's six sevens."],[2628.13,"So if you have six sevens, that's preparatory for a seventh seven."],[2633.11,"Like for a Sabbath."],[2634.4,"So here that's there's 40 years of the desert, that's preparatory."],[2638.72,"Meaning they're actually learning and growing and coming to know God better."],[2643.0,"And that's preparatory then for a Sabbath."],[2646.14,"For when they come and have rest in the land."],[2648.14,"John is showing us how that's a larger picture of our life in this world"],[2649.3,"St. Our life in this world, our whole life in this world is preparatory as we grow and learn and draw closer to God to prepare us for the Sabbath rest that's waiting for us in the kingdom of heaven."],[2666.9,"He's making that parallel."],[2668.18,"And he does that by way of in his gospel presenting the life of Jesus as a whole as preparatory to Christ resting in the tomb on the Sabbath and then the eighth day of the resurrection."],[2682.44,"So you have sort of the type or the image in the Old Testament with Israel in the wilderness."],[2688.92,"Christ embodies that himself in his own life, and then that describes our lives as followers of Christ, sort of in this third stage."],[2700.96,"So now, though we've had this second clarifying episode, God is now going to give a third sign to make it abundantly clear who Aaron is and where his authority comes from."],[2720.72,"Listen next time as Father Stephen DeYoung continues his study of the scriptures on the Whole Counsel of God."],[2728.08,"Father Stephen's email address is whole counsel at ancientfaith.com."],[2733.36,"That's whole counsel at ancientfaith.com."]],"o":[{"t":21.84,"lv":2,"h":"Where we are: Numbers 16","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Starting at the beginning of <b>Numbers 16</b></li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Numbers</b> = a mix of genres</li><li class=\"d1\">census data, commandments, <b>narrative stories</b> of Israel in the desert</li><li class=\"d1\">shifts back and forth rapidly</li><li class=\"d0\">Ch. 15 = mostly <b>commandments</b>; ch. 16 = <b>story</b> again</li><li class=\"d1\">don't need ch. 15 to follow the story</li><li class=\"d0\">Narrative setting: Israel told they'll spend <b>40 years in the desert</b></li><li class=\"d1\">rest of Numbers' narratives = incidents <b>during the 40 years</b></li><li class=\"d1\">no continuous narrative - \"this happened... years pass... another thing years later\"</li><li class=\"d1\">often not told <b>how much time</b> has passed</li></ul>"},{"t":161.93,"lv":2,"h":"Numbers 16:1-3 - Korah's rebellion","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>16:1</b> Korah, Dathan, Abiram, On rise up</li><li class=\"d0\">Genealogy = <b>generations skipped</b></li><li class=\"d1\">Levi = son of Jacob - far more than 3 generations back</li><li class=\"d1\">order of names: <b>personal name</b> (Korah) → <b>extended family</b> (Izhar) → <b>clan</b> (Kohath) → <b>tribe</b> (Levi)</li><li class=\"d1\">\"here's who he is, the family, clan, tribe he's part of\"</li><li class=\"d1\">Dathan and Abiram: family of Eliab, clan of On, tribe of <b>Reuben</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Korah = a <b>Levite</b>; Dathan and Abiram <b>not</b></li><li class=\"d0\"><b>16:2</b> 250 men - <b>rulers of the congregation</b>, \"men of note\"</li><li class=\"d1\">rough number, not precise</li><li class=\"d1\">prominent people from different clans and tribes</li></ul>"},{"t":305.57,"lv":3,"h":"Their argument: \"all are holy\"","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>16:3</b> \"all the congregation are <b>holy ones</b>, and the Lord is in them\" - why exalt yourselves?</li><li class=\"d0\">\"The first Protestants\" - little jab at Protestant friends</li><li class=\"d1\">all Israelites holy, God speaks to all, leads all</li><li class=\"d1\">who are you, Moses, to lead? Aaron, to be the only high priest, only your sons priests?</li><li class=\"d0\">Jewish saying: last time one side <b>100% right</b>, other <b>100% wrong</b> = <b>Moses vs. Korah</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Their argument isn't based on nothing</li><li class=\"d1\">Exodus: God called Israel a <b>kingdom of priests</b> to the nations</li><li class=\"d1\">but God also designated <b>certain tribes, clans, families</b> for roles</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>authority, hierarchy, structure</b> - that's what Korah attacks</li><li class=\"d0\">Claim: should be a <b>democracy</b>, everyone does everything</li><li class=\"d0\">Implied accusation: Moses and Aaron <b>seized</b> positions themselves</li><li class=\"d1\">denying that authority <b>comes from God</b></li></ul>"},{"t":461.57,"lv":2,"h":"Moses' response: God chooses","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>16:4-7</b> Moses <b>falls on his face</b></li><li class=\"d1\">show of <b>humility</b> - understands the accusation of ambition, \"lording it over us\"</li><li class=\"d0\">\"God examines and knows those who are his\" - brings them near</li><li class=\"d1\">\"near\" is literal: <b>high priest</b> → most holy place; <b>priests</b> → holy place</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>God chooses</b> who has authority - \"you don't just grasp it\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Test: bring <b>censers with fire and incense</b> tomorrow</li><li class=\"d1\">the man the Lord chooses = the holy one</li><li class=\"d1\">\"if God chooses you to be priests, you'll be priests; if someone else, accept it\"</li></ul>"},{"t":557.51,"lv":3,"h":"To the Levites: \"Is this a small thing?\"","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>16:8-11</b> Moses speaks to <b>Korah and the Levites</b> specifically</li><li class=\"d1\">Reubenites \"in a different category\"</li><li class=\"d0\">God separated you from Israel to serve the <b>liturgies</b>, stand before the congregation</li><li class=\"d1\">your family has a particular role</li><li class=\"d0\">\"Are you seeking the priesthood also?\" - \"Is that nothing to you?\"</li><li class=\"d1\">\"if you can't have that, forget the whole thing\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Especially concerning: God <b>did</b> give them a role, they want another</li><li class=\"d1\">because <b>more prestigious</b></li><li class=\"d0\">\"You and your company are against <b>God</b>\"</li><li class=\"d0\">\"Who is Aaron that you murmur against him?\"</li><li class=\"d1\">you're disputing with God</li><li class=\"d1\">what did Aaron ever do to you? He didn't take the high priesthood from you - just <b>serving as called</b></li></ul>"},{"t":674.26,"lv":2,"h":"Dathan and Abiram refuse","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>16:12-14</b> Moses <b>summons</b> the non-Levite leaders</li><li class=\"d1\">Levites nearby - Moses and Aaron are Levites, all camped together</li><li class=\"d0\">\"<b>We will not come up</b>\"</li><li class=\"d1\">parody of Moses' line: \"is this a small thing?\"</li><li class=\"d1\">\"brought us out of a <b>land flowing with milk and honey</b>\" - Egypt?! \"Was that what Egypt was like?\"</li><li class=\"d1\">makes no logical sense: <b>kill us in the desert</b> AND <b>rule over us</b> - tyrant or murderer?</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>16:14</b> \"would you <b>put out the eyes</b> of these men?\"</li><li class=\"d1\">accusation: Moses tortures, gouges out eyes of anyone who disagrees</li><li class=\"d1\">reality: God ready to destroy, Moses <b>interceding</b> again and again</li><li class=\"d1\">accusing him of the <b>exact opposite</b></li><li class=\"d0\">\"Pure derangement\" - \"we hate Moses\"</li><li class=\"d1\">accusations don't fit together, <b>no logical case</b></li></ul>"},{"t":832.73,"lv":2,"h":"Moses' appeal and the censer test","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>16:15</b> Moses \"very heavy of spirit\"</li><li class=\"d1\">to God: don't accept their sacrifice tomorrow</li><li class=\"d1\">\"I have not taken a desirable object... nor harmed any of them\"</li><li class=\"d1\">not getting rich off this - \"I don't understand why they hate me\"</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>16:16-17</b> Korah, company, Aaron: each takes <b>censer</b>, fire, incense</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>250 censers</b>, plus Aaron</li><li class=\"d1\">God will choose - \"tell us who's right\"</li></ul>"},{"t":896.85,"lv":2,"h":"Glory appears; Moses and Aaron intercede","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>16:18-19</b> All stand at the <b>tabernacle doors</b></li><li class=\"d1\">Korah's group at the <b>entrance</b>; Aaron and priests in the <b>courts</b></li><li class=\"d1\"><b>glory of the Lord</b> appears to all the congregation</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>16:20-22</b> God: \"<b>Separate yourselves</b>... I will utterly destroy them at once\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Moses and Aaron <b>fall on faces</b>: \"God of the spirits of all flesh, if <b>one man sins</b>, will wrath be on all the congregation?\"</li><li class=\"d1\">don't step back and say \"see, this is what happens when you mess with us\"</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>intercede again</b>: Korah's way out of line, but don't hold it against everybody</li><li class=\"d1\">even though the rest are gathered with him, on his side</li></ul>"},{"t":977.3,"lv":3,"h":"\"Get away from the tents\"","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>16:23-24</b> God: tell the congregation <b>withdraw</b> from Korah's company</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>16:25-26</b> Moses goes to Dathan and Abiram with the <b>elders</b></li><li class=\"d1\">\"Touch nothing of theirs lest you perish\"</li><li class=\"d1\">\"just how human\" - guy thinks \"they won't need this, I'll grab it\"</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>16:27</b> Dathan and Abiram stand at <b>tent doors</b> with wives, children</li><li class=\"d1\">fellow leaders: \"this isn't going how we thought\" - back off</li><li class=\"d1\">Korah = <b>set in his ways</b></li><li class=\"d1\">\"callous\" = <b>hard, stubborn</b></li></ul>"},{"t":1051.72,"lv":2,"h":"The sign: the earth swallows them","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>16:28-30</b> Moses: \"By this you shall know the Lord sent me\"</li><li class=\"d1\">\"I didn't take this authority for myself\" - God put me here</li><li class=\"d0\">If they <b>die naturally</b> → the Lord hasn't sent me</li><li class=\"d1\">if the earth <b>opens its mouth</b>, swallows them alive into <b>Hades</b> → they provoked the Lord</li><li class=\"d1\">Hades = the <b>underworld</b></li><li class=\"d0\"><b>16:31-33</b> As he finishes, the ground <b>splits</b></li><li class=\"d1\">swallows them, houses, men with Korah, tents</li><li class=\"d1\">earth covers them - <b>perished</b> from the congregation</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>16:34</b> All Israel flees at their cry: \"lest the earth swallow us\"</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>16:35</b> <b>Fire</b> from the Lord consumes the <b>250</b> offering incense</li><li class=\"d1\">irony: you offer incense by <b>burning</b> it</li><li class=\"d1\">Q: were they still offering while it happened? A: yes, at the gate - <b>didn't repent</b></li><li class=\"d1\">\"the <b>Nadab and Abihu</b> treatment\"</li></ul>"},{"t":1159.35,"lv":2,"h":"The sons of Korah","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>Psalms</b>: series before and after <b>Ps. 100</b> by the <b>sons of Korah</b> - same Korah</li><li class=\"d1\">talk of God preserving them from going down to <b>Hades / Sheol</b></li><li class=\"d1\">surviving household experienced <b>deliverance</b> from rebellion and sin</li><li class=\"d1\">preserved in <b>hymns</b>: rebellion, realizing where you're headed, <b>being rescued</b></li><li class=\"d0\">OT view: not God punishing for \"something bad\" but <b>consequences of actions</b></li><li class=\"d1\">Nadab and Abihu entered God's presence <b>sinfully</b>; so did these</li><li class=\"d1\">\"in their wickedness, <b>God's holiness consumed them</b> - like fire\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Some <b>distanced themselves</b> from Korah → <b>repented</b>, didn't suffer it</li><li class=\"d1\">fully committed → <b>death, destruction</b></li></ul>"},{"t":1297.77,"lv":2,"h":"Object lessons and the individualist view","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Earlier: <b>sticks on the Sabbath</b> - examples made of someone</li><li class=\"d0\">Modern <b>individualistic</b> perspective: \"did he really deserve that? kind of mean of God\"</li><li class=\"d0\">But rebellion against God → <b>destruction</b> as its end</li><li class=\"d1\">leaders were leading the <b>whole community</b> to destruction</li><li class=\"d1\">that'd be the consequence of <b>them getting their way</b></li><li class=\"d0\">God shows consequences <b>now</b> as a sign → message to everyone to <b>repent</b></li><li class=\"d1\">\"the death of these 250 <b>saves the lives of thousands</b>\"</li><li class=\"d0\">\"Went down into Hades\" ≠ went to hell</li><li class=\"d1\">just means <b>dead</b> - in Torah everybody dies, goes to <b>Sheol</b></li><li class=\"d1\">don't know their fate on the <b>day of judgment</b></li><li class=\"d1\">Korah was dead wrong - <b>not necessarily unpardonable</b> in the eternal sense</li><li class=\"d1\">others: don't know each one's relationship with God - just wrong about this one thing</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>sign</b> needed for everyone else because of the danger</li></ul>"},{"t":1454.01,"lv":3,"h":"Atheist objection and the resurrection","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Internet atheists: \"flood in Texas, people died, therefore no God\"</li><li class=\"d1\">unstated premises</li><li class=\"d0\">Odd Christian responses: <b>deny it's bad</b>, or \"God wasn't involved\"</li><li class=\"d1\">\"a lot of people dying in a flood <b>is bad</b>\" - not a mature understanding</li><li class=\"d0\">Atheist assumes God is responsible for all bad things</li><li class=\"d1\">but who is responsible if no God? why not if there is?</li><li class=\"d0\">Scripture: tells of <b>wars, massacres, plagues</b></li><li class=\"d1\">shows how God <b>brings good out of them</b> / they serve purposes</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Resurrection of the dead</b> → everyone raised on the last day</li><li class=\"d1\">good and bad in this world <b>not the final word</b></li><li class=\"d0\">\"Horrible thing the OT God does\" - <b>why</b> is it horrible?</li><li class=\"d1\">for Korah's sons later? the rest of Israel? Moses and Aaron, falsely accused?</li></ul>"},{"t":1617.62,"lv":3,"h":"\"Grow up\" - God is not an indulgent parent","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Against the \"<b>beautiful and unique snowflake</b>\" fantasy: \"candy and rainbows my whole life\"</li><li class=\"d1\">\"grow up\" - not a mature view of the world, of <b>my own sinfulness</b></li><li class=\"d1\">need to <b>learn, grow, face consequences</b></li><li class=\"d0\">God as <b>indulgent parent</b> = ridiculous - \"see how children of indulgent parents turn out\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Questions to ask: what is God doing for the <b>communal life</b> of the people?</li><li class=\"d1\">destructive activity + recruiting others → sometimes consequences must be <b>displayed</b></li><li class=\"d1\">parents do this; <b>courts</b> too - \"sometimes you <b>throw the book</b> at somebody\"</li><li class=\"d1\">impact bigger than just them</li><li class=\"d0\">\"The story isn't over yet\" - <b>gets worse before it gets better</b>, \"Spoilers\"</li></ul>"},{"t":1733.09,"lv":2,"h":"Numbers 16:36-40 - The censers become an altar covering","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>16:36-38</b> God to Moses and <b>Eleazar</b> the priest</li><li class=\"d1\">collect the <b>copper censors</b> from the burned</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>scatter the strange fire</b> - dump the incense out</li><li class=\"d1\">\"to <b>sanctify</b> the censers of those sinners\"</li><li class=\"d1\">beat into <b>plates as a covering for the altar</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Image of <b>forgiveness</b></li><li class=\"d1\">censers <b>not punished</b> - <b>cleansed, purified</b></li><li class=\"d1\">incense was the problem - they weren't to offer it</li><li class=\"d1\">Q: were they offering their own kind of incense? A: yes</li><li class=\"d1\">sin <b>removed</b> from a person; forgiveness = <b>washing away, purification</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Beaten into a covering for the altar - \"a <b>sign</b> to the children of Israel\"</li></ul>"},{"t":1828.99,"lv":3,"h":"Who is the reminder for?","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Seems: so people remember Korah, don't repeat it</li><li class=\"d1\">\"priestly authority is something God <b>gives</b>, not something you take\"</li><li class=\"d0\">But who sees the covering? <b>Altar of incense</b> in the <b>holy place</b></li><li class=\"d1\">only <b>priests</b> and high priests go in</li><li class=\"d1\">that's why <b>priests</b> make it - only ones who can attach it</li><li class=\"d1\">people already saw the story; <b>priests</b> are the ones reminded</li><li class=\"d0\">Authority = <b>double-edged sword</b></li><li class=\"d1\">Korah types want <b>prestige</b>, \"letters before and after their name\"</li><li class=\"d1\">don't want <b>responsibility, judgment</b></li><li class=\"d1\">St. Paul: \"not many of you should presume to be <b>teachers</b>\" - more accountable</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Accountability</b> chain on the day of judgment</li><li class=\"d1\">each: account for <b>yourself</b></li><li class=\"d1\">married: self and <b>spouse</b>; children: self, spouse, <b>children</b></li><li class=\"d1\">priest: self, spouse, children, \"<b>every one of you</b>\", the parish</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>bishop</b>: self, all his clergy and families, all people in every church he oversaw</li><li class=\"d1\">\"That's a heavy weight\"</li></ul>"},{"t":1972.14,"lv":3,"h":"The bishop's omophorion and the weight of authority","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Bishop's vestment: a <b>band over the shoulders</b>, around the back of the neck, hangs down</li><li class=\"d1\">represents the <b>weight of authority</b> taken on his shoulders</li><li class=\"d0\">People who ask \"why can't I do this?\" don't want the <b>heaviness</b></li><li class=\"d1\">want what they see from outside: <b>title</b>, asked for a <b>blessing</b></li><li class=\"d1\">not the <b>responsibility</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Covering = reminder to priests of the <b>seriousness, awesomeness, fearful task</b></li><li class=\"d1\"><b>accountability</b> each time they see <b>censers of false priests</b></li></ul>"},{"t":2059.12,"lv":2,"h":"Numbers 16:39-40 - Memorial, and the people murmur again","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>16:39-40</b> Eleazar adds the censers as <b>altar covering</b></li><li class=\"d1\">memorial: <b>no outsider</b> not of Aaron's seed puts incense before the Lord - \"be like Korah\"</li><li class=\"d0\">\"Issue dealt with?\" - not for our Israelite friends</li><li class=\"d1\">Q: like a cover on top? A: <b>attached to the sides</b> of the altar</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>16:41</b> <b>Next day</b> Israel murmurs: \"<b>You killed the people of the Lord</b>\"</li><li class=\"d1\">just saw earth swallow people, fire incinerate - still the <b>chutzpah</b></li><li class=\"d1\">\"good godly people who you killed\" - Moses = \"an <b>evil wizard</b>\"</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>16:42-43</b> Congregation regroups; <b>cloud</b> covers tabernacle, glory seen</li><li class=\"d1\">God visits: not \"grandpa coming over, let's play Scrabble\" - \"<b>wait till your dad gets home</b>\"</li><li class=\"d1\">\"chickens coming home to roost\"</li></ul>"},{"t":2202.34,"lv":2,"h":"Moses and Aaron intercede again","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>16:44-45</b> \"Get away... I will utterly destroy them at once\"</li><li class=\"d1\">\"apparently they didn't get the message yesterday\" → more <b>object lessons</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Moses and Aaron fall on faces - <b>interceding</b> for the people</li><li class=\"d1\">not God flying off the handle with Moses \"now, Skeeter, we don't want no trouble\"</li><li class=\"d1\">Moses and Aaron are <b>learning and growing</b> too</li><li class=\"d1\">again and again <b>humility</b> - \"more than I have\"</li><li class=\"d1\">\"third time... let's start over - I'd say sounds good\" - \"I am not a saint like Moses\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Moses: \"<b>please don't</b>\" - they gathered to murder me, <b>have mercy</b></li><li class=\"d1\">finding it within himself - <b>transformative</b> for Moses</li><li class=\"d1\">earlier in life: not so forgiving</li></ul>"},{"t":2330.08,"lv":2,"h":"Aaron's atonement with incense","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>16:46</b> Moses: take <b>censer</b>, fire from the <b>altar</b>, incense, run to the camp, <b>make atonement</b></li><li class=\"d1\">\"wrath has gone out... beginning to strike\"</li><li class=\"d1\">Aaron = the <b>rightful priest</b> - interceding <b>publicly</b></li><li class=\"d0\">People see <b>Aaron</b>, God's high priest, <b>standing in their midst</b> begging mercy</li><li class=\"d1\">day before: consequences didn't teach them</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>new approach</b> - Moses' idea, <b>God didn't tell him</b></li><li class=\"d1\">show: \"we're on their side, not the ones to hate\"</li><li class=\"d1\">high priest <b>doesn't lord it over</b> them - <b>intercedes before God</b></li><li class=\"d1\">\"do it publicly, in the middle of them\"</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>16:47-48</b> Aaron runs in; plague already begun</li><li class=\"d1\">incense, atonement; <b>stood between the dead and the living</b> → plague <b>ceased</b></li><li class=\"d1\">place he stands/intercedes = where destruction <b>stops</b></li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Incense purifies</b> → atonement = <b>purifying</b> from consequence of sin</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>16:49-50</b> <b>14,700</b> died besides Korah's; Aaron returns to Moses at the door</li></ul>"},{"t":2494.24,"lv":2,"h":"Signs in Numbers and John","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">\"Another sign\" - Numbers describes miracles as <b>signs</b></li><li class=\"d1\"><b>ten plagues</b> not called signs in the same way</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>Gospel of John</b> calls Christ's miracles <b>signs</b></li><li class=\"d1\">Matthew, Mark, Luke: just miracles, healings</li><li class=\"d0\">More ahead: <b>bronze serpent</b> lifted in the wilderness → Christ refers to it in <b>John</b></li><li class=\"d0\">John: Jesus' authority <b>like Moses'</b></li><li class=\"d1\">life in this world = a <b>sojourn</b> through the wilderness</li><li class=\"d1\">signs from God enter through Christ - show the <b>path</b></li><li class=\"d0\"><b>40</b> = <b>preparation</b> (40 days, 40 years)</li><li class=\"d1\">actually <b>42 = six sevens</b> → preparatory for a <b>seventh seven</b> = <b>Sabbath</b></li><li class=\"d1\">wilderness = learning, <b>knowing God better</b> → <b>rest in the land</b></li><li class=\"d0\">John: whole life here preparatory for <b>Sabbath rest in the kingdom of heaven</b></li><li class=\"d1\">Jesus' life preparatory to <b>resting in the tomb on the Sabbath</b>, then the <b>eighth day</b></li><li class=\"d1\">type in Israel → Christ embodies → <b>our lives as followers</b> (third stage)</li><li class=\"d1\">after this <b>second clarifying episode</b>, God will give a <b>third sign</b> - to make clear <b>who Aaron is</b> and where his authority comes from</li></ul>"}],"next":"Next time: a <b>third sign</b> to make clear who Aaron is and where his authority comes from"});
